      "content": "Actually, enemy plant like this rarely act \"mysteriously\" without a clear cause, so environmental factors are a strong suspect. Recent changes in light levels, temperature fluctuations, sudden humidity drops, or even a draft could trigger this response so quickly. You might want to check if the plant was moved to a different corner or if a new pet entered the room recently to rule out those shifts. The sudden onset is actually quite common when the roots get stressed from poor drainage for too long.",
